  "notes": "COMPOUND VERB STRUCTURE: {溜|た}める (to save/accumulate) + {込|こ}む (to put into)\n\nTRANSITIVITY: Transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}). Takes an object marked with を.\n\nCONJUGATION: Godan verb (-む type)\n- {溜|た}め{込|こ}まない (negative)\n- {溜|た}め{込|こ}みます (polite)\n- {溜|た}め{込|こ}んで (te-form)\n- {溜|た}め{込|こ}んだ (past)\n\nUSAGE:\n{溜|た}め{込|こ}む often has a slightly negative connotation, suggesting excessive accumulation or hoarding. Compare with {溜|た}める which is more neutral.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ストレスを{溜|た}め{込|こ}む - to bottle up stress\n- {不満|ふまん}を{溜|た}め{込|こ}む - to accumulate frustration\n- {物|もの}を{溜|た}め{込|こ}む - to hoard things\n- {仕事|しごと}を{溜|た}め{込|こ}む - to let work pile up\n\nREGISTER:\nNeutral. Common in everyday conversation.",
